<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: NEGATIVE TWIN of synth-ubl-good-intra-community_ubl.xml.
     Byte-for-byte identical to that clean intra-community-supply invoice EXCEPT
     the Buyer VAT identifier (BT-48) is removed: the customer's
     cac:PartyTaxScheme[VAT]/cbc:CompanyID (FR00000000000) is deleted.

     For an intra-community supply (VAT category K) BR-IC-02 mandates that an
     invoice carrying a K invoice line SHALL have BOTH a VAT-scoped Seller
     identifier (BT-31, still present: DE000000000) AND the Buyer VAT identifier
     (BT-48). With BT-48 gone, that seller-AND-buyer conjunction is broken, so
     the ONLY fired rule is BR-IC-02 (fatal). The arithmetic is untouched (VAT
     total 0.00, taxable = Σ K nets, tax inclusive = tax exclusive all still
     reconcile) and the K exemption reason (VATEX-EU-IC), the actual delivery
     date (BR-IC-11) and the deliver-to country (BR-IC-12) are all intact, so no
     BR-CO totals rule and no other BR-IC rule fires. Exactly one distinct fatal,
     isolating the BR-IC-02 shape: valid=false, exit 1. -->
